# L §4.2, §8.4 (tally 2.1.7 B5, issue #98; R5): a duration that isn't a whole number of an index's keys is
# refused where load sees it and the index's step, LOAD-DOMAIN with run's words: q + 1 year on a year index by 2.
# Twin: L4_2_by_n_duration_run. 2.1.6's refcore answered it (2027-01-01).
=== load.tally
model b5
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "made up"

index y2 = year 2026..2040 by 2

input n1: int

def bad[q in y2]: date = start_of(q + 1 year)

ask a_bad: bad[2026]

version v
  cite plan
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n1 = 1 "one"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DOMAIN q + 1 year: not a whole number of its periods (L §4.2) ...
